From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:53:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] EGL: return the driver entry from eglGetProcAddress with slow
 binding

Under USE_SLOW_BINDING the extension forwarders (getProcAddress.cpp
__glExtFwd*) still read TP + TLS_SLOT_OPENGL_API in inline asm, with no
generic variant. Return the driver's address instead of the forwarder.

Precondition: one GL driver per process. The forwarder only switches
the extension entry per bound context's connection; both GLESv1 and
GLESv2 hooks get the same addr here, so with one driver the result is
the same function. Re-check when a second driver (ANGLE for ES1) loads.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [glibc hosts only]
Patch-Reason: the forwarders are naked per-arch asm reading the thread pointer, which on glibc is glibc's TCB; no loader or environment setting reaches them, and a generic C forwarder cannot pass arbitrary arguments through.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 opengl/libs/EGL/egl_platform_entries.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/opengl/libs/EGL/egl_platform_entries.cpp b/opengl/libs/EGL/egl_platform_entries.cpp
index 6713a5c69d27618157c7b0da495f96c332cd021c..99a6e194ec5baf39d3079dfaa862899adf47b7c7 100644
--- a/opengl/libs/EGL/egl_platform_entries.cpp
+++ b/opengl/libs/EGL/egl_platform_entries.cpp
@@ -1243,7 +1243,9 @@ __eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType eglGetProcAddressImpl(const char* procn
                     // Track the top most entry point return the extension forwarder
                     cnx->hooks[egl_connection_t::GLESv1_INDEX]->ext.extensions[slot] =
                             cnx->hooks[egl_connection_t::GLESv2_INDEX]->ext.extensions[slot] = addr;
+#if !USE_SLOW_BINDING
                     addr = gExtensionForwarders[slot];
+#endif
 
                     // Remember the slot for this extension
                     extensionSlotMap[name] = slot;
@@ -1275,7 +1277,9 @@ __eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType eglGetProcAddressImpl(const char* procn
         // Track the top most entry point and return the extension forwarder
         cnx->hooks[egl_connection_t::GLESv1_INDEX]->ext.extensions[ext_slot] =
                 cnx->hooks[egl_connection_t::GLESv2_INDEX]->ext.extensions[ext_slot] = addr;
+#if !USE_SLOW_BINDING
         addr = gExtensionForwarders[ext_slot];
+#endif
     }
 
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&sExtensionMapMutex);
